// Package tui is the pi-tui helper surface of the Go extension SDK: the pure functions and values a Pi extension imports from
// @earendil-works/pi-tui to draw its own components. A custom Render(width) measures, wraps, truncates and slices ANSI text with
// these, matches raw terminal input against key identifiers, and styles text with the same color helpers as Pi.
//
// Every function follows Pi's own implementation at the pinned release byte for byte. The vectors in test/parity/sdk-bulk are
// generated by running Pi's functions (utils.ts, keys.ts, fuzzy.ts, colors.ts, terminal-image.ts) and every SDK reproduces them.
// Names mirror upstream's with Go capitalization; where Go cannot hold both Pi's function and Pi's type of one name, the type takes a
// Result suffix (fuzzyMatch returns FuzzyMatchResult).
//
// The engines live in internal/ as generated copies of the application's own tui package (see tui/sdk_tui_copy_test.go in the main
// module): the SDK module cannot import the application.
package tui
